.TH "EPX\-SITES" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-sites \- read, create and change sites and their mixins
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites [flags]
epx sites [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads active sites. Inactive sites are not included: Emporix returns them only with the write\-capable site.site_manage scope, so \fBget CODE\fR of an inactive site is refused (403, exit 3) without it. \fBepx sites codes\fR lists the codes of every site, inactive ones too (opt\-in); to read inactive sites whole, run \fBepx api get \(aq/site/{tenant}/sites?includeInactive=true\(aq \-\-scope site.site_manage\fR.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the site.site_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx sites codes"
List the codes of every site, inactive ones too.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites codes [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the code of every site, active or not. Emporix lists inactive sites only with the write\-capable site.site_manage and site.site_read scopes together (each alone answers 403), so this read is opt\-in; \fBepx sites list\fR shows active sites whole without a scope. Emporix sends no total for the codes, so their pages are read until an empty one.
.PP
Requires the site.site_read, site.site_manage scopes. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR
Opt in to requesting site.site_read, site.site_manage, which can also change data (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx sites create"
Create a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a site from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as \fBepx sites get CODE \-o json\fR prints one. The reference requires code, name, defaultLanguage, languages, currency, homeBase (an address with country and zipCode), shipToCountries and taxDeterminationBasedOn (BILLING_ADDRESS or SHIPPING_ADDRESS); active, default, includesTax, availableCurrencies, payment, shipping, tax, mixins and cartCalculationScale are optional.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx sites delete"
Delete a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites delete CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the site CODE; it sends no body. Emporix refuses to delete the default site. An unknown CODE is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type CODE at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx sites get"
Show one site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites get CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads active sites. Inactive sites are not included: Emporix returns them only with the write\-capable site.site_manage scope, so \fBget CODE\fR of an inactive site is refused (403, exit 3) without it. \fBepx sites codes\fR lists the codes of every site, inactive ones too (opt\-in); to read inactive sites whole, run \fBepx api get \(aq/site/{tenant}/sites?includeInactive=true\(aq \-\-scope site.site_manage\fR.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CODE, NAME, DEFAULT, LANGUAGES, CURRENCY, HOME, SHIPS TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
