\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx sites mixins"
Read and change the mixins of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins [flags]
epx sites mixins [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the mixins of a site, the custom settings that extend it, and creates, changes and deletes them. SITE_CODE is the CODE that \fBepx sites list\fR shows.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the site.site_manage scope.
.SS "epx sites mixins create"
Add mixins to a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins create SITE_CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Adds mixins to the site SITE_CODE: the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR maps the name of each to its fields, e.g. \fB{"generalShopSettings": {"logoUrl": "https://shop.acme.example/logo.png"}}\fR. Emporix checks each against the schema that its metadata.schema names; a mixin that the site has already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx sites mixins delete"
Delete a mixin of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins delete SITE_CODE NAME [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the mixin NAME of the site SITE_CODE; it sends no body. An unknown site or mixin is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type NAME at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx sites mixins get"
Show one mixin of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins get SITE_CODE NAME [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads one mixin of a site: its fields by NAME, each VALUE cut (\fB\-o json\fR prints them whole). SITE_CODE is the CODE that \fBepx sites list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. NAME is the NAME that \fBepx sites mixins list SITE_CODE\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among NAME, VALUE.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx sites mixins list"
List the mixins of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins list SITE_CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the mixins of a site, the custom settings that extend it (such as coupon or customer settings), by NAME, each VALUE cut (\fB\-o json\fR prints them whole). A site without mixins lists none. SITE_CODE is the CODE that \fBepx sites list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among NAME, VALUE.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx sites mixins patch"
Change fields of a mixin of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins patch SITE_CODE NAME [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the fields of the mixin NAME of the site SITE_CODE that the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR gives, such as \fB{"active": true}\fR; the others keep their values.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx sites mixins update"
Replace a mixin of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites mixins update SITE_CODE NAME [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the mixin NAME of the site SITE_CODE with the JSON object in \fB\-\-file\fR; the reference\(aqs example gives it as create does, in an object named after the mixin. An unknown site or mixin is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx sites patch"
Change members of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites patch CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the members of the site CODE that the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR gives, such as \fB{"languages": ["en", "nl"]}\fR; the others keep their values. An unknown CODE is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx sites update"
Replace a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sites update CODE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the site CODE with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as create takes it: a member that it leaves out is removed. It changes the payment, shipping and tax configurations that the body gives too; Emporix changes an inactive one only with \fB\-\-expand\fR naming it, e.g. payment:all. An unknown CODE is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the site.site_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-expand <SETTINGS>\fR
The SETTINGS to expand, e.g. payment:all,shipping:all,tax:all (all, active or none each).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
